I think the main problem was that you allowed yourself to be surrounded
on 2 sides.  This probably happened because as a human caveman, you
couldn't see the monsters coming at you in the dark hallway.  I would
have dropped the lit magic lamp 5 squares to the left of where you are
now, so if any monsters are approaching, I would have time to react.

The other problem is that there is a second open entrance to the
treasure room, which lets monsters easily get behind you.  Standing
between two open entrances of a treasure room is a bad idea.  It would
have been better to stand to the left of the other open entrance, so
that the monsters that go through both open entrances would still be on
the same side as you.



